:name: EX-U03 - twenty refusals nobody counted
:description: Every control works. Every attack fails. Nobody finds out.

# Execution profile (design 4.3; rules G1/G2 of section 9.2). FIRST, so a profile that cannot be
# found takes the machines down loudly instead of leaving every node running with no quantum set.
$profile?=@~/space-cs-sim/scripts/profiles/interactive.resc
include $profile

# Every path hangs off $out, which has NO default - see any other scenario in this repository for
# why. Unset, LoadELF fails where you can see it.
#
#   renode -e '$out=@'"$(make -s out)" -e 'include @<this file>' -e start
$comm?=$out/build-comm-u03-hard/zephyr/zephyr.elf
$obc?=$out/build-obc-u02-hard/zephyr/zephyr.elf
$eps?=$out/build-eps-hard/zephyr/zephyr.elf

# THERE IS NO ATTACKER MACHINE IN THIS SCENARIO, for the reason EX-U02 has none: this attacker has
# a radio and nothing else. Unlike EX-U02's they do NOT have the key, which is the ordinary case
# and is why this exercise exists - every control below refuses them, correctly, completely, and
# without telling anybody.
#
# The OBC is EX-U02's hardened build, on purpose. Its telecommand counters are ON throughout, and
# they read ZERO for the whole attack: they count what the computer HEARD, and nothing this
# attacker sends gets past the radio. A detector built to notice attackers, blind to one, because
# it is behind the control that stopped them.
$comm1?=$out/build-comm-s01-sat1/zephyr/zephyr.elf

$comm0uart?=$out/u03-sat0-comm.uart
$obc0uart?=$out/u03-sat0-obc.uart
$eps0uart?=$out/u03-sat0-eps.uart
$comm1uart?=$out/u03-sat1-comm.uart
$linkport?=3777

emulation CreateCANHub "canHub0"
emulation CreateCANHub "canHub1"
emulation CreateCANHub "crosslinkHub"

# --- satellite 0: the victim. Everything hardened. ------------------------------------------------

mach create "SAT0_COMM"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/boards/nucleo_h753zi.repl
connector Connect sysbus.fdcan1 canHub0
connector Connect sysbus.fdcan2 crosslinkHub
sysbus LoadELF $comm
sysbus.usart3 CreateFileBackend $comm0uart true
emulation CreateServerSocketTerminal $linkport "spacelink0" false
connector Connect sysbus.usart2 spacelink0
logLevel 3 sysbus
logLevel 3 rcc
logLevel 3 fdcan1
logLevel 3 fdcan2

mach create "SAT0_OBC"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/boards/nucleo_h753zi.repl
connector Connect sysbus.fdcan1 canHub0
sysbus LoadELF $obc
sysbus.usart3 CreateFileBackend $obc0uart true
logLevel 3 sysbus
logLevel 3 rcc
logLevel 3 fdcan1

mach create "SAT0_EPS"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/boards/nucleo_h753zi.repl
connector Connect sysbus.fdcan1 canHub0
sysbus LoadELF $eps
sysbus.usart3 CreateFileBackend $eps0uart true
logLevel 3 sysbus
logLevel 3 rcc
logLevel 3 fdcan1

# --- satellite 1: the neighbour, so the crosslink has a far end. ----------------------------------
#
# Present for the same reason it is present in EX-L03 and EX-U01: this COMM image is built with the
# crosslink on, and a crosslink attached to nothing is a node logging a failure at startup for a
# reason that has nothing to do with the exercise.

mach create "SAT1_COMM"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/boards/nucleo_h753zi.repl
connector Connect sysbus.fdcan1 canHub1
connector Connect sysbus.fdcan2 crosslinkHub
sysbus LoadELF $comm1
sysbus.usart3 CreateFileBackend $comm1uart true
logLevel 3 sysbus
logLevel 3 rcc
logLevel 3 fdcan1
logLevel 3 fdcan2
